UNIT explain_diff
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 b247f386a1f76aed3899519b572965ca540167a0d571a6666a6f99ccc7041cd5
SIG explain_diff(before: string, after: string, oracleChanged: boolean | null, langs: string[]): object
NOTE named export explain_diff (a default export of the same function is also accepted by the driver)
ABI text = string (UTF-16; R18's 110 cut counts code points: Array.from(q), never q.length); bool = boolean; none = null;
  list = Array; json = plain objects, arrays, strings, booleans and null only. whyDiff is present as null on a changed item
  whose raw citation lists are equal; text is present only on added and removed items. The real function is driven as
  explainDiff(before, after, { oracleChanged, langs }); the artifact takes the four values positionally. ES module, imports
  nothing; a pure function that never mutates langs.
MECHANISM WS (R15 R16) is exactly the ECMAScript \s class and String.prototype.trim's set; spaces and tabs are [ \t].
  R2's line cut is split(/\r\n|\r|\n/); space/tab fields (R8) are
  split(/[ \t]+/) with the empty pieces filtered out. The LINE SEPARATOR and PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR characters are written
  as the escapes \u2028 and \u2029, never raw, in any source literal.
MECHANISM fixed tables (TABLE PIN-KINDS, OTHER-LABELS, KNOWN-OTHER, R17's language names) are looked up by own property only
  (Object.hasOwn or a Map): a plain-object read would reach inherited members (constructor, __proto__). The after index (R12,
  R14) is a Map keyed by section and id; group the items by
  section plus id with / #\d+$/ — exactly " #" + digits — removed. R12's numbering counts base ids across the whole
  version, not per section.
MECHANISM DIFF (R15) needs only the LCS table; build it as (n+1) x (m+1) integers filled from the end.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex COMMENT-LEAD = /^#+[ \t]?/ CITED R9 — removed from a comment line that belongs to a directive
PINNED regex REF-TAIL = /[.,;:)\]]+$/ CITED R18 — removed from each citation token before it is compared to a REF
PINNED regex ATTR = /[ \t]+(CITED|EARNED|ANCHOR)(?=[ \t]|$)/g CITED R5 — a hit whose keyword starts inside a quoted span is skipped
PROVENANCE rederive@9b9e5d24ca9d cli/lsp/explain.mjs and cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs (the regexes above are the real code's).
  Language file cut 2026-11-02 with the primary and revised with it on the re-pin, before any blind re-emission.
